  "details": "First and foremost, I have to ask what it means.If an avatar fails, a security check or has a question mark when you're trying to load it.\n\nAlso because of the age of some of the avatars, there was a joke. Avatar, made by bruce lee 117 call average anime girl.\n\nThere was no explicit features on the avatar.Nor was there anything that could be considered illegal under german law.\n\nBut I wish there was a way to contest some of these avatar .\n\nbans.  And sometimes the creators, well, things just rot, and I have a very sensitive spot when it comes to that.\n\nEven if it's like a game shutting down or something loss is loss. Could there be a way to contest some of these removals and bans? And if not a way to contest them, get the reason why things are happening?  \n\nMaybe more transparency when it comes to the moderation process? Or maybe you are already transparent.But it's hard to see exactly what's being moderated for why?And what. In fact, the names of the avatars and everything else are totally unavailable.So you don't even know what you're missing. Or what you've lost.",
